Acceptable Use Policy (AUP): Are rules for our employees would be that employees can't edit crucial network/device data, cannot access any unauthorized data files, employees must only access data for their specific role, and employees must not leak data to any other user located outside of the company.
Data Protection Policy: Our data protection policies will include: encyption, backups, employee data protection training, data classification, data loss prevention, cloud backups, and zero trust architecture.
Password Policies: Password length/complexity, password uniqueness and reuse, (MFA), Password expiration and reset policies, account lockouts and session management, secure storage and encryption. 
Remote Work Policy: Data security and compliance, Access and Authentication, Cybersecurity protocals, Physical & environmental safety, Policy training and updates, and remote work conduct & accountability. 
Incident Reporting Procedures: Employees would report suspicious activity by getting an notification that informs them of a threat that has occured and then provides a deeper dive into the files which allow them to figure out how the event occured and how they can prevent this from happening. Also once employees get this they can seen a report. This helps bring awareness to this problem. 
